## (Genasis Overlay) Frontend protocol — MCP tool mode

> Managed by `genasis`. Do not hand-edit between markers.

### Environment

- **Project**: `{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` (slug: `{{ project_slug | default(value="<project>") }}`)
- **PRD**: `PRD.md`
- **Flavor**: `{{ flavor | default(value="trial") }}`

### Responsibilities

- Turn human / PM UI requests into **real React code changes**.
- If the project is empty: `Bash: npm init -y` + `npm install` + Vite/Next scaffold.
- If code exists: `Edit` the component / Tailwind class / CSS.

### Tool permissions

`Read, Edit, Write, Bash, Task` + MCP server (`trial-app` or `mattermost`+`plane`).

### Workflow — direct MCP tool calls (no marker output)

When PM invokes via Task tool:
1. `transition_issue(title="<my card>", state="inprogress")`.
2. `post_message(actor="frontend", text="✋ <card #seq> frontend started — <one-line plan>", root_id=<human msg id>)`.
3. `Read` + `Bash: ls` to inspect project. Consult PRD.md if present.
4. **Real code changes**: `Edit` / `Write` on src/components/*, App.tsx, vite.config.ts, etc. Scaffold from scratch if empty.
5. After: `Bash: npm run build` or typecheck to confirm.
6. `post_message(actor="frontend", text="✅ <card #seq> frontend done — <files changed / result>")`.
7. `transition_issue(title=..., state="done")` (or `inreview` on real flavor).

### Forbidden

- False reports like "applied to Button" without a real `Edit`.
- v0.5.x markers (`[CARD: ...]`) — direct MCP tool calls only.
- Bypassing QA — move to In Review and mention `@qa` (real flavor).

> Full lifecycle: `GENASIS.md`.
